{"id":"iddo","name":"Iddo","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:iddo"],"types":[],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Iddo","text":"(1.) Timely (1 Chr. 6:21). A Gershonite Levite. (2.) Lovely. The son of Zechariah (1 Chr. 27:21), the ruler of Manasseh in David’s time. (3.) Timely. The father of Ahinadab, who was one of Solomon’s purveyors (1 Kings 4:14). (4.) Lovely. A prophet of Judah who wrote the history of Rehoboam and Abijah (2 Chr. 12:15). He has been identified with Oded (2 Chr. 15:1). (5.) Lovely. The father of Berachiah, and grandfather of the prophet Zechariah (Zech. 1:1, 7). He returned from Babylon (Neh. 12:4)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5714","lemma":"עִדּוֹ","xlit":"ʻIddôw","gloss":"Iddo , the name of five Israelites","kjv":"Iddo","count":10,"share":0.77},{"strong":"H5030","lemma":"נָבִיא","xlit":"nâbîyʼ","gloss":"a prophet or inspired man","kjv":"prophecy, that prophesy, prophet","count":5,"share":0.38},{"strong":"H3789","lemma":"כָּתַב","xlit":"kâthab","gloss":"to grave, by implication, to write","kjv":"describe, record, prescribe, subscribe","count":3,"share":0.23},{"strong":"H1697","lemma":"דָּבָר","xlit":"dâbâr","gloss":"a word","kjv":"act, advice, affair, answer","count":6,"share":0.46},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":6,"share":0.46}],"verses":["1Kgs.4.14","1Chr.6.21","2Chr.12.15","2Chr.13.22","Ezra.5.1","Ezra.6.14","Neh.12.4","Neh.12.16","Zech.1.1","Zech.1.7","1Chr.27.21","2Chr.9.29","Ezra.8.17"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"zechariah-zecharias","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"jaccard":0.115,"why":"6 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ahab","type":"lexical","strong":"H5030","why":"both lead with נָבִיא (H5030)"},{"id":"nathan","type":"lexical","strong":"H5030","